("> ⚠ **Tool caveat.** APIs named here (`userEvent.setup({ advanceTimers })`, `vi.useFakeTimers`, `vi.setSystemTime`, Testing Library `configure({ reactStrictMode })`, Vitest `sequence.shuffle`, Stryker configuration) are as commonly documented at the time of writing; **verify against current docs** for your installed versions.",
 "> **Tool note (verified 2026-10-22).** `userEvent.setup({ advanceTimers })` and `delay`, `vi.useFakeTimers`/`vi.setSystemTime`, Testing Library `configure({ reactStrictMode })` and Vitest `--sequence.shuffle`/`--sequence.seed` were checked by running them on Vitest 3.2.7, RTL 16.3.3 and user-event 14.6.8 (details in lessons 03-05). **Important:** under Vitest, `advanceTimers` alone does *not* stop `user.*`/`findBy*`/`waitFor` from hanging with fake timers (RTL's own async wrapper also waits on a faked `setTimeout`); see the fix in §3.3. Stryker was not run here; check its docs (Stryker 10 is current)."),
("so with fake timers a plain `await user.click()` can hang unless user-event is told how to advance time:\n\n```ts\nvi.useFakeTimers();\nconst user = userEvent.setup({ advanceTimers: vi.advanceTimersByTime }); // (verify in user-event docs)\n```\nAlternatively `vi.useFakeTimers({ shouldAdvanceTime: true })` lets fake time advance with real time.",
 "so with fake timers a plain `await user.click()` hangs. **Telling user-event how to advance time is necessary but not sufficient with Vitest** (verified): RTL's `asyncWrapper`, used by every `user.*` call and by `findBy*`/`waitFor`, also waits on a faked `setTimeout(0)` and only auto-advances when a global `jest` exists. Working setup:\n\n```ts\nbeforeEach(() => {\n  vi.stubGlobal('jest', { advanceTimersByTime: vi.advanceTimersByTime.bind(vi) }); // makes Testing Library advance Vitest's fake time\n  vi.useFakeTimers();\n});\nafterEach(() => { vi.useRealTimers(); vi.unstubAllGlobals(); });\n\nconst user = userEvent.setup({ advanceTimers: vi.advanceTimersByTime }); // option name verified\n```\nAlternatively `vi.useFakeTimers({ shouldAdvanceTime: true })` lets fake time advance with real time (it unblocks everything but makes exact-millisecond assertions racy), or fake only what the code needs and leave `setTimeout` real. Full table of variants and results: [lesson 04 §3.4](./04-testing-async-updates.md)."),
("test('debounces search by 300ms and sends only the latest query', async () => {\n  vi.useFakeTimers();\n  const user = userEvent.setup({ advanceTimers: vi.advanceTimersByTime });",
 "test('debounces search by 300ms and sends only the latest query', async () => {\n  vi.stubGlobal('jest', { advanceTimersByTime: vi.advanceTimersByTime.bind(vi) });   // see §3.3: without this, user.type hangs under vi.useFakeTimers()\n  vi.useFakeTimers();\n  const user = userEvent.setup({ advanceTimers: vi.advanceTimersByTime });"),
("  vi.useRealTimers();                                // better in afterEach to run even on failure\n});","  vi.useRealTimers();                                // better in afterEach (with vi.unstubAllGlobals()) to run even on failure\n});"),
("(it re-exports React's `act`; verify)","(it wraps React's `act`)"),
("⚠ TanStack Query option names (`gcTime` vs older `cacheTime`) depend on version: verify.","TanStack Query v5 uses `gcTime` (v4 called it `cacheTime`)."),
("⚠ `findByRole('listitem', { name })` requires list items to have an accessible name; `listitem` role's name is not computed from content in all implementations (naming from content applies to some roles, not `listitem`).","`findByRole('listitem', { name })` requires list items to have an accessible name; `listitem` does not get its name from content (verified on DTL 10.4.2: `getByRole('listitem', { name: 'Ada Lovelace' })` found nothing for `<li>Ada Lovelace</li>`)."),
